{"task_id": "HumanEval/22", "solution": "from typing import List, Any\n\n\ndef filter_integers(values: List[Any]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\" Filter given list of any python values only for integers\n    >>> filter_integers(['a', 3.14, 5])\n    [5]\n    >>> filter_integers([1, 2, 3, 'abc', {}, []])\n    [1, 2, 3]\n    \"\"\"\nHere's the code continuation:\n\n```python\n    return [x for x in values if isinstance(x, int) and not isinstance(x, bool)]\n```\n\nThe function filters the input list to keep only integers. Note that we need to exclude booleans with `not isinstance(x, bool)` because in Python, `bool` is a subclass of `int`, so `isinstance(True, int)` returns `True`."}
